    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 60 tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July, named by its ending calendar year \u2014 Australian convention, so a 2026-08-17 registration falls in **FY27**).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a canonical `static int fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` helper (month \u2265 July \u2192 year+1, else year) and a derived `getFiscalYear()` returning `\"FY<YY>\"` from the registration date. Switched the tenure point rule in `getMembershipPoints()` from `> 365` days to \"at least one elapsed fiscal year\" (`fiscalYearOf(now) - fiscalYearOf(registrationDate) >= 1`). A new owner still has zero tenure, so the level-4 invariant holds. Removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import and updated the surrounding docstrings.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `assignMembershipNumber` now derives the `-M<YY>` segment from `Owner.fiscalYearOf(...)` instead of the calendar year, so the membership number's year segment matches `fiscalYear`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` mapping so the derived value is exposed in the response DTO.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec) and updated the `membershipNumber`, `membershipPoints`, and `membershipLevel` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nThe two spec tests confirm the behaviour: `Cp48` (response returns `fiscalYear` matching `FY\\d{2}`) and `Cp14` (membership number's `-M<YY>` equals the `fiscalYear` digits). All existing tests remain green.",
